      "changed_decision": "yes",
      "explanation": "Without historical evidence, the question might appear straightforward to test with sequence counts from the graph database. The retrieved records establish that: (a) the only prior attempt to look at teammate DRIVE→PNR found a negative, not positive, premium; and (b) the play-type labels used suffer from systematic foul leakage that undermines any drive-based analysis. These findings shift the decision from 'proceed with careful design' to 'do not proceed until measurement reliability is resolved'."
